<title>SWITZERLAND: Swiss Life details group 1996 results.</title>
<headline>Swiss Life details group 1996 results.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>				    (million Sfr unless stated)</p>
<p> Gross premiums		 13,878	    vs 10,834</p>
<p> Earned premiums*	     13,481	    vs 10,608</p>
<p> Net investment income	4,910	     vs 3,854</p>
<p> Claims incurred*	     7,587	     vs 6,424</p>
<p> Bonuses and rebates*	 1,455	     vs 1,413</p>
<p>Changes in technical</p>
<p>   provisions*		  7,465	     vs 5,146</p>
<p> Net operating expenses     1,558	     vs 1,294</p>
<p> Surplus			  1,509	     vs 1,306</p>
<p> Total assets		   88,101	    vs 73,615</p>
<p> New business written	 94,152	    vs 66,574</p>
<p> Business in force	    516,111	   vs 380,975</p>
<p> Number of staff		7,933	     vvs 7,661</p>
<p>* figure is net of reinsurance</p>
<p>NOTE - Company's full name is Swiss Life/Rentenanstalt . The company plans to transform into a public limited company from a cooperative, providing members approve.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
